fix(docker): make healthchecks robust + add /api/health endpoint

db (postgres) healthcheck:
  - Was: single-line "pg_isready -U ${POSTGRES_USER:-flamekeeper} ..."
    Compose interpolates env vars, but CMD-SHELL is more reliable than
    CMD for non-Windows binaries inside the container, and lets us use $
    to defer expansion to the container's shell.
  - Now: CMD-SHELL with $$-escaped args, retries 5->10,
    start_period 10s->20s.

flamekeeper app healthcheck:
  - Switched from /api/settings (admin-gated) to /api/health (public):
      GET /api/health         -> { status: "ok" }                  (cheap liveness)
      GET /api/health?deep=1  -> + Prisma SELECT 1; 503 if DB down
  - start_period 20s -> 60s (first boot runs init-db + seed).

README updated.